<title>UK: NEWCASTLE BUILDING SOCIETY H1 PROFITS FALL.</title>
<headline>NEWCASTLE BUILDING SOCIETY H1 PROFITS FALL.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's mutually-owned Newcastle Building Society said on Tuesday its first-half pre-tax profit fell to 4.46 million stg from 6.42 million stg in the year-earlier period.</p>
<p>Provisions for bad and doubtful debts decreased to 419,000 stg in the six months to June 30 from 1.34 million stg, the company said.</p>
<p>Newcastle awarded about 740,000 stg to borrowers who qualified under its loyalty bonus scheme, compared to 390,000 a year earlier.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
